  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Understanding how to cook eggs perfectly shows mastery of a deceptively simple skill. Eggs respond to precise technique, and knowing how to control them demonstrates cooking fundamentals. For date night, serving flawless eggs at breakfast shows confidence and capability that sets a positive tone."
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "icon": "💡",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**What you'll learn:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Universal principles for perfect eggs",
        "Temperature and timing for each method",
        "Common mistakes and how to avoid them",
        "Which preparations work best for different situations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Why Eggs Matter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Eggs are a fundamental cooking skill. They're quick, versatile, and unforgiving of mistakes. When you can cook eggs properly, it signals control over heat, timing, and technique."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "For morning-after breakfast or brunch dates, perfectly cooked eggs show you have cooking skills beyond dinner preparation. It's an unexpected competency that impresses."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://file.notion.so/f/f/b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5/8d5d6993-2e11-4766-b6f9-05ff121f4be9/vudememe_eggs_in_the_kitchen_hand_drawn_water_color_style_illus_d7f51efd-180b-4f01-9fec-22bcec542e75.png?table=block&id=2f7c3484-e8de-8056-943f-ea8339447641&spaceId=b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5&expirationTimestamp=1777291200000&signature=9i2ujqiuAdJ__8VhlIAWqR2dsfAq04Nf4qhWOFrInDY",
      "caption": null,
      "localPath": "src/assets/images/articles/the-foolproof-egg-formula.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The Universal Principles"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Principle 1: Low and Slow"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Eggs cook fast. High heat creates rubbery, overcooked results. Low to medium-low heat gives you control."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Principle 2: Remove Before Done"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Carryover cooking continues after you remove eggs from heat. Pull them slightly underdone."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Principle 3: Fresh Matters"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Fresh eggs (under 2 weeks old) have firmer whites and taller yolks. They fry and poach better."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Principle 4: Room Temperature"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Cold eggs straight from fridge cook unevenly. Let sit 10 minutes before cooking."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Scrambled Eggs (The French Method)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Creamy, custard-like texture that shows technique."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Ingredients (per person)"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "3 eggs",
        "1 tablespoon butter",
        "Salt and pepper",
        "Optional: 1 tablespoon cream or crème fraîche"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 1: Whisk eggs thoroughly**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Break up proteins completely. No streaks of white."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 2: Heat pan on medium-low**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Add butter, let melt but not brown."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 3: Add eggs**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Pour in, let sit 10 seconds."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 4: Stir constantly with silicone spatula**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Figure-eight pattern, scraping bottom and sides. 3-5 minutes total."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 5: Remove at soft curds**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Still slightly wet and glossy. They'll continue cooking."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 6: Serve immediately**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Add cream or butter off heat if desired. Season."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Result:** Silky, creamy eggs with small, soft curds."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://file.notion.so/f/f/b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5/9bdab3a8-a518-4f7c-b454-05949ff357ef/vudememe_scrambled_eggs_hand_drawn_water_color_style_illustrati_d9c067c2-4e39-43c8-b172-c1c0cf7c5000.png?table=block&id=2f7c3484-e8de-8036-87b8-ce2d76252671&spaceId=b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5&expirationTimestamp=1777291200000&signature=4mU-j9TZXtkqK6lwt3ygSf7txHqrx3EoHdESijiPTRU",
      "caption": null,
      "localPath": "src/assets/images/articles/the-foolproof-egg-formula-1.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Fried Eggs (Crispy Edges, Runny Yolk)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Classic preparation that requires heat control."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 1: Heat pan medium-high**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Add 1-2 tablespoons butter or oil."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 2: Crack eggs into small bowl first**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ensures no shell pieces, easier to slide into pan."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 3: Slide eggs into hot fat**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Should sizzle immediately."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 4: Let cook undisturbed (2-3 minutes)**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Whites set, edges get crispy and brown."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 5: Baste with hot fat or cover briefly**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "For over-easy: flip gently for 30 seconds."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "For sunny-side up: baste top with hot butter or cover 30 seconds to set white."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 6: Season and serve**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Salt and pepper after cooking."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Target:** White fully set, yolk warm and runny."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://file.notion.so/f/f/b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5/e300e29d-b90c-407e-94f3-5067faef1c93/vudememe_fried_eggs_hand_drawn_water_color_style_illustration_n_d11ae690-6fc8-475c-848a-db5561837ea2.png?table=block&id=2f7c3484-e8de-8068-85e1-cad9817c1784&spaceId=b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5&expirationTimestamp=1777291200000&signature=Hbq4pAALjn-LJa0-zABdKq0aYaMuNEKB9lbBfz5F6C8",
      "caption": null,
      "localPath": "src/assets/images/articles/the-foolproof-egg-formula-2.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Poached Eggs (Elegant, Difficult to Master)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Impressive technique that shows skill."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 1: Fresh eggs only**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Old eggs spread in water. Fresh eggs hold together."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 2: Bring water to bare simmer**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Tiny bubbles, not rolling boil. Add 1 tablespoon vinegar (helps whites coagulate)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 3: Create gentle whirlpool**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Stir water in circle with spoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 4: Crack egg into small bowl**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Slide into center of whirlpool gently."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 5: Cook 3-4 minutes**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "White fully set, yolk soft."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 6: Remove with slotted spoon**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Drain on paper towel briefly."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Tip:** Practice this alone first. It takes attempts to master."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://file.notion.so/f/f/b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5/ec0b92c2-6455-4ae6-9f89-38b08fce939e/vudememe_poached_egg_in_benedictine__hand_drawn_water_color_sty_a7c7f647-2436-4b71-b820-3ead4891a9a5.png?table=block&id=2f7c3484-e8de-806e-aeb9-febcb9879a24&spaceId=b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5&expirationTimestamp=1777291200000&signature=DgOKJX1w0CO-lM3cxXVkaPkxfTK9gIf9NYQfa23GcDw",
      "caption": null,
      "localPath": "src/assets/images/articles/the-foolproof-egg-formula-3.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Soft-Boiled Eggs (Jammy Yolk)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Consistent, foolproof, impressive presentation."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Method"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 1: Room temperature eggs**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Cold eggs crack in boiling water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 2: Boiling water**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Full rolling boil in pot."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 3: Lower eggs gently**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Use spoon or egg basket."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 4: Set timer**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "6 minutes: Liquid yolk, set white",
        "7 minutes: Jammy, custard-like yolk (ideal)",
        "8 minutes: Fully set but still soft"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 5: Ice bath immediately**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Stop cooking process."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Step 6: Peel under running water**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Start from wide end where air pocket is."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Serve:** Halved on toast, in ramen, or alone with salt."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://file.notion.so/f/f/b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5/1f5becdb-6e45-4d60-bf10-95eea8a82913/vudememe_soft_boiled_egg_hand_drawn_water_color_style_illustrat_b511baa0-d939-4f1e-874b-8e054e355238.png?table=block&id=2f7c3484-e8de-8066-ae2e-dbf66e8588f8&spaceId=b6fc3484-e8de-81e3-b238-00031f3692d5&expirationTimestamp=1777291200000&signature=HGfLkdY7J3zKMV-6C8M68GhZq4UZvS9avI-8NtUYMN0",
      "caption": null,
      "localPath": "src/assets/images/articles/the-foolproof-egg-formula-4.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Omelets (French vs. American)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "French Omelet"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Texture:** Smooth exterior, creamy inside, no browning"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Method:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Beat eggs with fork",
        "Medium heat, butter",
        "Constantly shake pan while stirring with fork",
        "Roll onto plate when still slightly wet"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time:** 60-90 seconds total"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Best for:** Showing technique, elegant brunch"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "American Omelet"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Texture:** Slightly browned, fully cooked, sturdy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Method:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Beat eggs",
        "Medium heat, butter",
        "Let set 30 seconds",
        "Lift edges, tilt to let uncooked egg flow under",
        "Add fillings when mostly set",
        "Fold in half"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time:** 3-4 minutes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Best for:** Heartier breakfast, holds fillings better"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Common Mistakes"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "❌ **High heat**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "✅ Medium-low for scrambled, medium for fried. Eggs need gentle heat."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "❌ **Overcooking**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "✅ Remove before fully set. They continue cooking."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "❌ **Stirring scrambled eggs too aggressively**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "✅ Gentle, constant motion creates small curds."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "❌ **Old eggs for poaching**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "✅ Fresh eggs (under 1 week) hold together best."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "❌ **Not preheating pan**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "✅ Eggs need immediate heat to set properly."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Date Night Applications"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Morning After Breakfast"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Making perfect eggs the morning after a date shows:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "You're comfortable and capable in the kitchen",
        "You pay attention to technique and details",
        "You can create something special with simple ingredients"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Soft scrambled eggs or a perfect omelet demonstrates skill without showing off."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Brunch Date"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Brunch invites call for impressive egg dishes:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Eggs Benedict (poached eggs, hollandaise)",
        "Shakshuka (eggs poached in spicy tomato sauce)",
        "Frittata (baked egg dish, serves multiple)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "These show you can handle more complex preparations."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Quick Reference Times"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Scrambled (French style):** 3-5 minutes, medium-low heat"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Fried (sunny-side up):** 2-3 minutes, medium-high heat"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Poached:** 3-4 minutes, bare simmer"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Soft-boiled (jammy):** 7 minutes, boiling water"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**French omelet:** 60-90 seconds, medium heat"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**American omelet:** 3-4 minutes, medium heat"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Pro Tips"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "For Scrambled Eggs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Add cream or butter at the very end, off heat",
        "Season after cooking (salt draws out moisture)",
        "Use silicone spatula for gentle stirring"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "For Fried Eggs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Butter browns and adds flavor, oil stays neutral",
        "Tilt pan to pool fat for basting",
        "Cover briefly if you don't want to flip"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "For Poached Eggs"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Strain raw egg through fine sieve first (removes loose whites)",
        "Multiple eggs: poach in batches, rewarm in hot water",
        "Make ahead: poach, store in ice water, reheat when needed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: How do I know if eggs are fresh?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Float test: Fresh eggs sink in water. Old eggs float. Or check the sell-by date (use within 3-4 weeks of laying)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: Why do my scrambled eggs get watery?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Overcooked. The proteins squeeze out moisture. Remove from heat earlier."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: Can I make poached eggs ahead?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Yes. Poach, store in ice water in fridge. Reheat 1 minute in simmering water before serving."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: What's the green ring around hard-boiled yolk?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Overcooked. It's harmless iron sulfide. Use shorter cooking time and ice bath immediately."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Q: Does adding milk to scrambled eggs help?**"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "No. It dilutes flavor and makes them watery. Use cream sparingly or none at all."
    },
    {
      "type": "divider"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The Skill Signal"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Perfectly cooked eggs are a reliable indicator of cooking skill. Chefs use egg tests in interviews because eggs don't lie. When you serve flawless eggs, it shows control, patience, and understanding of fundamentals."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "For morning-after breakfast, this skill shows thoughtfulness. You're not just throwing together food, you're applying technique to make something special."
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "icon": "✅",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Master one method first:**"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "ordered",
      "items": [
        "Choose scrambled eggs (most forgiving)",
        "Practice 3 times alone",
        "Low heat, constant stirring",
        "Remove when still slightly wet",
